mcpp for Debian
---------------

MCPP is a portable C preprocessor developed by Kiyoshi Matsui.
Please hava a look at: URL: http://www.m17n.org/mcpp/

Installation on Debian changes its executable name to "mcpp"
(originally, "cpp_std"), and only installs "standard" version.

MCPP has other three variants, K&R, pre ANSI standard, and post
standard version.  Those variants are not supported in this release.
Possibly, those will be supported in future release.

MCPP could be used as a replacement of GCC's cpp. This installation is
not the replacement installation, but the installation as a stand
alone program, /usr/bin/mcpp.

